    <h1>Corporate &amp; Global Mobility</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Immigration support for organisations moving talent into the Philippines.</p>

    <p>Bringing foreign talent into a Philippine operation, whether a single specialist hire or a growing international team, involves immigration requirements that run alongside your organisation's own hiring, assignment and compliance processes. Foreign Immigration Services works directly with employers, coordinating the immigration side of these matters for one employee or across an organisation's broader foreign workforce.</p>

    <div class="feature-image">
      <img src="/assets/images/corporate-global-mobility-feature.webp" alt="A corporate team coordinating foreign workforce matters in a modern Manila office." width="1536" height="1024">
    </div>

    <div class="proposition-highlight">
      <h2>One Immigration Partner for Your Foreign Workforce</h2>
      <p>Whether your organisation is bringing in a single specialist or coordinating immigration matters across a growing foreign workforce, FIS can act as a central point of coordination between your organisation and the foreign nationals you employ. We assess the appropriate pathway, coordinate the requirements between employer and employee, organise the supporting documentation, and manage the process on your behalf, where permitted, so your organisation is not starting from scratch with every hire, transfer or renewal.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Assessing the appropriate immigration and work-authorisation pathway for a proposed hire, transfer or assignment</li>
      <li>Coordinating the information and documentation required from both the employer and the foreign national</li>
      <li>Mapping the applicable requirements, including where a 9(g) Pre-Arranged Employment Visa or a specialised corporate pathway applies</li>
      <li>Preparing and organising the required documentation, and reviewing it for apparent gaps before submission</li>
      <li>Coordinating employment-permit requirements, including liaising with the Department of Labor and Employment where an Alien Employment Permit is a prerequisite</li>
      <li>Liaising with the Bureau of Immigration on your organisation's behalf, where representation is permitted</li>
      <li>Submitting or lodging applications, where applicable and permitted</li>
      <li>Following up on applications and keeping your organisation and the foreign national informed</li>
      <li>Coordinating renewals and continuing immigration requirements as they arise</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9(g) Pre-Arranged Employment Visas</h2>
    <p>The 9(g) Pre-Arranged Employment Visa is a principal immigration pathway for foreign nationals taking up pre-arranged employment with a Philippine-registered employer. Depending on the circumstances, the employment and immigration process may also involve an Alien Employment Permit or other applicable work-authorisation requirements. FIS can coordinate the relevant requirements with the sponsoring employer and foreign national, including the documentation and connected employment and immigration processes involved.</p>

    <h2>Specialised Pathways for Qualifying Corporate Personnel</h2>
    <p>Depending on the organisation, the employee's role and the applicable regulatory framework, a corporate assignment may involve an immigration pathway other than 9(g). Foreign executives and specialised personnel employed by a multinational company's regional or area headquarters in the Philippines, or by an enterprise registered with the Philippine Economic Zone Authority (PEZA), the Board of Investments (BOI) or another investment-promotion agency, may qualify for a distinct visa category, depending on the employer's registration, the employee's role and the applicable rules. Employer registration alone does not automatically extend to every employee. FIS can assess whether a specialised pathway appears applicable to your organisation's circumstances and coordinate the corresponding immigration requirements.</p>

    <h2>Ongoing Immigration Support for Your Foreign Workforce</h2>
    <p>Where an organisation employs more than one foreign national, or expects to hire, transfer or renew foreign employees over time, FIS can act as a standing point of contact rather than a one-off resource. This can include onboarding new foreign hires, coordinating upcoming renewals or extensions across your existing foreign employees, and managing several immigration matters at different stages at the same time.</p>

    <h2>Common Situations We Handle</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Hiring a foreign national for a role with your organisation</li>
      <li>Transferring an executive or specialist into a Philippine operation</li>
      <li>Bringing technical or specialised personnel into a Philippine-based team</li>
      <li>Coordinating immigration matters for several foreign employees at once</li>
      <li>Renewals or extensions coming due across your foreign workforce</li>
      <li>Uncertain whether 9(g) or a specialised corporate pathway applies to a role</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the Process Works</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Tell Us About Your Organisation and Personnel</h3>
        <p>Tell us about your organisation, the role or assignment, and the foreign national or nationals involved.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Pathway Assessment</h3>
        <p>We assess the circumstances and identify the immigration and work-authorisation pathway that may apply, based on the information available.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Employer &amp; Employee Documentation</h3>
        <p>We map the applicable requirements and coordinate the required documentation between your organisation and the foreign national.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Application Coordination</h3>
        <p>Where applicable and permitted, we coordinate and submit the application on your organisation's behalf.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Follow-Up &amp; Ongoing Requirements</h3>
        <p>We follow up on the matter and keep your organisation informed. You can track the progress of your transaction through the FIS Client Portal, and we can remain your point of contact for renewals and future immigration requirements.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What We May Need From You</h2>
    <h3>From Your Organisation</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Company and registration information relevant to the role</li>
      <li>Details of the role, assignment or transfer</li>
      <li>Employment contract, assignment letter or other employer-issued documentation, where applicable</li>
      <li>Relevant PEZA, BOI or other registration details, where applicable</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>From the Foreign National</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Passport and current immigration status</li>
      <li>Qualifications or employment records relevant to the role, where applicable</li>
      <li>Existing Philippine immigration or work-authorisation documentation, where applicable</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The specific documents required depend on the pathway, your organisation's structure and the foreign national's circumstances. We will confirm exactly what applies once we understand your situation.</p>

    <div class="context-note">
